// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Death Seeker
// @category Death Tropes / Character
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Death_Seeker
// @domain   Narrative
// @scale    arc
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): after loss, dishonor, or guilt they cannot repay, a character courts death —
// throwing themselves into battle after battle hoping for an honorable end — but proves far too good at
// surviving. FRONTIER: the will to die that won't be granted. The discriminator is a [+DeathWish]
// character bound on the agent of a [&CourtsDeath] event: actively seeking the end. Distinct from the
// suicidal (who would just do it) and the Determinator (who fights TO live): this one fights to die.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc death_seeker -> [
  redemption_equals_death : "often hopes for a",
  determinator : "the inverted will of",
  despair_event_horizon : "a standing aftermath of a"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the will to die, sought in battle, is the discriminator; promotion model) —
prop DeathWish   [+Psychological]   // longing for one's own (honorable) death after loss or guilt
verb CourtsDeath [+Psychological]   // throws oneself into mortal danger hoping to be killed

imply DeathSeeker -> [Psychological, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (arc scale): a [+DeathWish] character COURTS DEATH — the death-seeker bound on the agent
// role of a [&CourtsDeath] event, so phase-2 re-checks [+DeathWish] on the seeker (STYLE §8). Binding the
// will-to-die on the one hurling himself at danger is the discriminator: he fights to be killed, parting
// it from the Determinator (who fights to live) and a plain suicide (who would not need the battle).
rule Death_Seeker {
  when:
    char $c [+DeathWish]
    evt  $charge [&CourtsDeath(agent=$c)]
  then:
    $charge [+DeathSeeker]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Logan — the weary Wolverine (film, 2017) ===
// Logan is old, poisoned by his own adamantium, everyone he loved long dead; the healing factor that
// once made him immortal is failing, and part of him welcomes it. He drinks, he picks fights he half
// hopes to lose, he throws his ruined body into battles a younger man would avoid — courting the death
// that has been denied him for two centuries. He is not suicidal so much as ready, hurling himself at the
// end and, to his weary frustration, surviving anyway.

// LOGAN / WOLVERINE — old, failing, half in love with his own end
char logan [+Protagonist] [+DeathWish]

scene the_last_fight {
  beat 1 {
    // he throws his ruined body into a battle, half-hoping not to walk away
    evt the_charge [&CourtsDeath(agent=logan)]
    // Death_Seeker -> the_charge [+DeathSeeker]
  }
}
